Code statements included in point 1 should be as brief as possible, only include the ones that are most related to the root cause and  the number of code statements may not exceed 3.


Here is the commit message:
SOLR-1095: fix stopword and keep filter performance issue

git-svn-id: https://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/lucene/solr/trunk@761036 13f79535-47bb-0310-9956-ffa450edef68

Here is the root cause:
The performance issue was primarily due to the use of `HashSet` for storing stop words and keep words, which is less efficient for the operations being performed. The initialization and processing of these sets were not optimized, leading to slower performance when handling large lists of words. The changes made to use `CharArraySet` instead significantly improve the performance of the filtering process.

Here is the patch:
 import org.apache.lucene.analysis.StopAnalyzer;
 import org.apache.lucene.analysis.TokenStream;
